1
00:00:04,603 --> 00:00:12,543
Book an appointment — Scheduling ▸ Calendar — Create, find and change an appointment — and understand what the type controls.

2
00:00:17,925 --> 00:00:27,020
Scheduling ▸ Calendar is the practice diary — every provider, every room.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:33,172
Day view for working the desk hour by hour.

4
00:00:33,172 --> 00:00:39,626
Week view for spotting the gaps worth filling.

5
00:00:39,626 --> 00:00:46,617
Every booking answers four questions: who, what, with whom, and when.

6
00:00:46,617 --> 00:00:54,542
Who. Start typing or pick from the register — the MRN disambiguates namesakes.

7
00:00:54,542 --> 00:01:02,020
What. The appointment type sets the duration for you — change the type, not the clock.

8
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:08,920
With whom. Only providers who work that day are offered.

9
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:16,785
When. Pick the slot; the duration follows the type you chose.

10
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:24,645
A one-line reason is what the clinician reads before the patient walks in.

11
00:01:24,645 --> 00:01:33,896
A confirmation step, so a mis-click never books a patient.

12
00:01:33,896 --> 00:01:42,813
Booked. The slot fills on the calendar and the patient gets their reminder.

13
00:01:42,813 --> 00:01:49,127
The List view is the same diary as a searchable table — where you change or cancel a booking.

14
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:56,640
Cancelling keeps the record and its reason. Deleting would erase the history — so cancel, do not delete.

15
00:01:58,453 --> 00:02:11,323
What you just did

16
00:02:11,981 --> 00:02:20,981
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
